 ### CRITICAL: Async Applications (FastAPI, etc.)
 
-**The Databricks SDK is fully synchronous.** All calls block the thread. In async applications (FastAPI, asyncio), you MUST wrap SDK calls with `asyncio.to_thread()` to avoid blocking the event loop.
+Treat synchronous SDK network calls and iterator consumption as blocking unless
+the selected API explicitly provides async behavior. Keep blocking work off an async
+event loop using the application's chosen worker boundary; `asyncio.to_thread()`
+below is one option. Bound concurrency and client lifetimes, consume lazy iterators
+inside the worker, and account for cancellation: cancelling the await does not
+necessarily stop an SDK request already running in a thread. Preserve the selected
+timeout/retry policy instead of layering unbounded application retries.
 
